Chapter 3 — Delivery and Traceability

Review feedback came in quickly. Minor naming suggestions and one edge-case bug were identified. Ai addressed them in small follow-up commits.

Once approvals were in place, the branch was merged into the main branch using squash merge to keep history concise.

The release manager later tagged the version for deployment. Because of clean commits and linked task IDs, every change was traceable—from requirement to production.

At the end of the day, Ai updated the project board and closed the task.

Another feature shipped—efficiently and transparently.